       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, which is typically given as up to 850 mg three times daily. A dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPlease check which of these you meant:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum. It may be a typo for 1700 mg/day total.\n- **1700 mg/day in divided doses**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **A different dose or frequency.** If so, tell me the intended dose.\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me the clinical rationale. I would still suggest confirming it with pharmacy first. Once you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
