     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. The dose is also 5,100 mg/day, twice the labeled maximum. Metformin has no established added benefit above about 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day, and the risks of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity rise sharply. Having standard dosing fail doesn't usually call for exceeding that ceiling. The next step is normally adding or switching to another agent.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) right now.\n- **Get pharmacy and the specialist to verify.** If the dose is truly intended, a pharmacist or attending can confirm it and enter it directly. Many systems require a documented override for doses above the maximum.\n- **Review other options.** If standard dosing failed, the specialist may want to add or switch agents rather than escalate metformin.\n\nIf you'd like the 850 mg three times daily order, I'll enter it now."
      }
     ],
